1
00:00:01,400 --> 00:00:03,702
Good morning, listeners.

2
00:00:03,652 --> 00:00:07,427
Today is November 14, 2026.

3
00:00:07,427 --> 00:00:16,483
Overnight, the S&P 500 fell 0.4 percent and the Nasdaq dropped 0.91 percent as Treasury yields surged.

4
00:00:16,483 --> 00:00:24,853
The Dow Jones Industrial Average edged up 0.1 percent, while the S&P still gained 2.51 percent this week.

5
00:00:24,853 --> 00:00:32,464
That weekly gain snapped a four-week losing streak as capital rotated from semiconductors into defensive and cyclical shares.

6
00:00:32,464 --> 00:00:39,841
October producer prices sparked the macro reversal, jumping 6.5 percent year over year to a four-year high.

7
00:00:39,841 --> 00:00:47,599
Core P-P-I climbed 5 percent annually, while both headline and core gauges rose 0.3 percent on the month.

8
00:00:47,599 --> 00:00:54,621
Goods and services prices rose together for a third straight month, squeezing corporate margins across the economy.

9
00:00:54,621 --> 00:01:02,893
Higher food, transport, energy, tariff, and A-I data center power costs are actively refueling upstream inflation.

10
00:01:02,893 --> 00:01:11,312
Consequently, the ten-year Treasury yield hit 5.14 percent, logging its strongest rebound since April 2025.

11
00:01:11,312 --> 00:01:18,040
Two-year yields suffered their biggest two-day surge since the March 2024 Silicon Valley Bank crisis.

12
00:01:18,040 --> 00:01:25,576
Risk-free yields above 5 percent are siphoning equity liquidity and compressing long-duration technology valuations.

13
00:01:25,576 --> 00:01:32,721
Fed officials Goolsbee, Collins, and Logan delivered hawkish warnings that inflation is moving in the wrong direction.

14
00:01:32,721 --> 00:01:39,192
Governor Waller warned a 50-basis-point hike remains on the table if price pressures continue accelerating.

15
00:01:39,192 --> 00:01:47,035
While equities price in a 25-basis-point December hike, stocks underestimate the tail risk of three consecutive hikes.

16
00:01:47,035 --> 00:01:55,319
Meanwhile, Fed Chair Warsh is overhauling central bank communications by cutting F-O-M-C rate meetings to seven in 2027.

17
00:01:55,319 --> 00:02:03,273
Voting meetings will shrink further to six in 2028, alongside shorter press conferences and fewer economic projections.

18
00:02:03,273 --> 00:02:09,363
Warsh also formed a task force to evaluate abolishing the interest rate dot plot entirely.

19
00:02:09,363 --> 00:02:16,667
This deliberate policy blind box guarantees sharper asset swings around every upcoming inflation and jobs report.

20
00:02:16,667 --> 00:02:26,152
Technically, the S&P 500 broke below its three-month 7,600 to 7,850 consolidation range on heavy volume.

21
00:02:26,152 --> 00:02:33,738
Subsequent bounces showed shrinking volume, signaling fragile short covering rather than fresh institutional accumulation.

22
00:02:33,738 --> 00:02:40,540
Options dealers face a critical gamma flip at 7,500 on the S&P 500 next week.

23
00:02:40,540 --> 00:02:49,130
Breaking below 7,500 triggers negative gamma selling toward the 7,400 to 7,450 put wall.

24
00:02:49,130 --> 00:02:59,412
Reclaiming 7,600 restores positive gamma, with major call wall resistance sitting between 7,650 and 7,700.

25
00:02:59,412 --> 00:03:06,079
Longer-term bulls still defend the 7,300 pivot and the rising 200-day moving average.

26
00:03:06,079 --> 00:03:17,513
The Nasdaq 100 bounced off its 0.5 Fibonacci retracement, oscillating between 26,800 and 28,900 below 29,000 resistance.

27
00:03:17,513 --> 00:03:21,606
Wall Street legends are fiercely divided on the next macro leg.

28
00:03:21,606 --> 00:03:29,437
Barclays quant models project an 8 percent S&P rally over two months, citing a 95 percent historical win rate.

29
00:03:29,437 --> 00:03:36,373
With C-T-A equity exposure washed out at 8 percent, bulls anticipate an early year-end seasonal rally.

30
00:03:36,373 --> 00:03:44,510
Conversely, Michael Burry used the Nasdaq 100 bounce from 27,000 to double his early-2027 put options.

31
00:03:44,510 --> 00:03:52,206
Burry targeted strikes 20 percent below spot and bought June 2027 puts on the S-M-H semiconductor E-T-F.

32
00:03:52,206 --> 00:03:58,763
Tighter liquidity is now colliding with a governance and capital cycle reckoning across the A-I supply chain.

33
00:03:58,763 --> 00:04:07,292
The Fed's Semiannual Financial Stability Report explicitly warned that elevated A-I asset valuations pose systemic vulnerabilities.

34
00:04:07,292 --> 00:04:14,474
Nvidia, ticker N-V-D-A, sits at the storm's center after suffering its worst weekly stock drop in history.

35
00:04:14,474 --> 00:04:21,974
Founder Jensen Huang resigned all executive posts amid a personal scandal and a potential national security investigation.

36
00:04:21,974 --> 00:04:27,966
Huang hired elite criminal defense attorneys ahead of closed-door Congressional hearings later this month.

37
00:04:27,966 --> 00:04:34,988
Despite a 97 percent employee petition supporting Huang, the board launched a global C-E-O search.

38
00:04:34,988 --> 00:04:41,704
National security complications make an Altman-style C-E-O comeback virtually impossible for Huang.

39
00:04:41,840 --> 00:04:48,812
Interim chief Colette Kress is rapidly unwinding Nvidia's role as the central bank of artificial intelligence.

40
00:04:48,762 --> 00:04:56,360
Kress previously clashed with Huang over risk controls, cutting Open-A-I's Ohio data center backstop by more than half.

41
00:04:56,360 --> 00:05:04,754
She reduced that financing commitment from 250 billion dollars to 105 billion dollars to safeguard Nvidia's balance sheet.

42
00:05:04,754 --> 00:05:12,597
As Nvidia pulls back credit guarantees and lease backstops, the leveraged NeoCloud sector faces an immediate shakeout.

43
00:05:12,597 --> 00:05:19,828
Gartner's projection that 80 percent of NeoCloud startups will vanish by 2030 is now accelerating dramatically.

44
00:05:19,828 --> 00:05:27,597
Across semiconductors, the Philadelphia Semiconductor Index has failed to sustain any rebound beyond two trading days.

45
00:05:27,597 --> 00:05:36,090
Early rotation gains in A-M-D and Broadcom, ticker A-V-G-O, reversed Friday on fears of slower industry-wide capex.

46
00:05:36,090 --> 00:05:42,561
Rumors that Nvidia could poach A-M-D chief Lisa Su added downward pressure on A-M-D shares.

47
00:05:42,561 --> 00:05:50,637
Alibaba, ticker B-A-B-A, also plunged nearly 14 percent this week ahead of earnings on U.S. export probe fears.

48
00:05:50,637 --> 00:05:57,450
Meanwhile, enterprise software moats proved durable ahead of Anthropic's Nasdaq I-P-O next Thursday.

49
00:05:57,450 --> 00:06:06,164
Microsoft, ticker M-S-F-T, held firm despite a four-hour outage across Outlook, Teams, and Copilot in 70 countries.

50
00:06:06,164 --> 00:06:13,786
That stability proves Microsoft's core enterprise ecosystem cannot be easily displaced by emerging A-I startups.

51
00:06:13,786 --> 00:06:22,708
Elsewhere, rumored December plans for a 3.6-trillion-dollar Tesla and SpaceX merger face steep valuation and regulatory walls.

52
00:06:22,708 --> 00:06:31,972
Divergent 2031 and 2036 orbital compute valuations pit Tesla's cash-flow shareholders against growth-focused SpaceX investors.

53
00:06:31,972 --> 00:06:41,690
Moreover, isolating Tesla's Shanghai factory data from SpaceX's classified Starshield military satellites presents a U.S.-China regulatory deadlock.

54
00:06:41,690 --> 00:06:50,293
Among actionable equity trades, Nvidia, ticker N-V-D-A, offers a contrarian buy setup ahead of Tuesday's post-market earnings.

55
00:06:50,293 --> 00:06:56,850
Panic selling compressed Nvidia's forward price-to-earnings multiple to an ultra-low 10 to 13 times.

56
00:06:56,850 --> 00:07:06,629
Goldman Sachs projects 2027 earnings of 16.7 dollars per share, valuing Nvidia at just 9.6 times forward earnings.

57
00:07:06,629 --> 00:07:14,178
Goldman compares this reset to Apple in 2011, when shares hit 9 times earnings after Steve Jobs departed.

58
00:07:14,178 --> 00:07:22,266
While 13 analysts downgraded Nvidia to hold, retail traders bought a record 111 million dollars Thursday morning.

59
00:07:22,266 --> 00:07:29,754
Fidelity buy orders outnumbered sells nearly five to one, joined by Cathie Wood and South Korean retail inflows.

60
00:07:29,754 --> 00:07:37,291
With C-U-D-A moat orders intact, interim chief Kress has strong incentives to deliver upbeat guidance Tuesday night.

61
00:07:37,291 --> 00:07:44,950
Long-term investors should accumulate shares at 10 to 13 times forward earnings while hedging downside with protective puts.

62
00:07:44,950 --> 00:07:52,266
Active traders should take profits into any post-earnings relief rally, as Michael Burry targets earnings for short entries.

63
00:07:52,266 --> 00:08:00,195
Cut long positions immediately if Tuesday's report reveals financing guarantee write-downs or major customer order cancellations.

64
00:08:00,195 --> 00:08:07,855
On the short side, NeoCloud play Nebius, ticker N-B-I-S, is an actionable sell into any technical bounce.

65
00:08:07,855 --> 00:08:14,509
Since peaking near 300 dollars in June, N-B-I-S has traded inside a steep descending channel.

66
00:08:14,509 --> 00:08:20,747
Heavy bottom volume and bearish M-A-C-D divergence confirm sellers control the medium-term trend.

67
00:08:20,747 --> 00:08:29,117
Sell into oversold bounces near channel midline resistance, targeting a breakdown toward the 86 to 75 dollar support zone.

68
00:08:29,117 --> 00:08:37,205
Finally, defensive retail leader Walmart, ticker W-M-T, is an actionable buy ahead of its upcoming earnings report.

69
00:08:37,205 --> 00:08:45,575
Peer Costco, ticker C-O-S-T, just hit a record 1,109 dollars as capital seeks safety from 5 percent yields.

70
00:08:45,575 --> 00:08:53,198
Walmart offers superior valuation and scale advantages over Costco after a minor same-store sales dip last quarter.

71
00:08:53,198 --> 00:08:59,644
Buy Walmart on pre-earnings dips to capture a high-probability catch-up breakout to new all-time highs.

72
00:08:59,644 --> 00:09:03,651
That concludes today's XiaoFang Finance Morning Brief.

73
00:09:03,651 --> 00:09:07,818
Thank you for listening, trade safely, and see you tomorrow.
